ay fine an  investigation has started  but it's going to find nothing and then  it's okay the investigation did lead to  some indictments but they're not related  to anything Trump did or knew about the  goal posts keep moving here's another  example  at first it was of course there's no  collusion and then it became collusion  wouldn't necessarily be illegal and with  obstruction of justice the goalposts  moving is it used to be obstruction of  justice no way nohow  put it out of your mind and now the  conversation has shifted to even if the  president obstructed justice the  president can't actually be charged with  that because they are President of the  United States that's a new conversation  where the goal posts have been moved so  far that they're in the locker room or  the parking lot of the stadium arguing  that you couldn't possibly be charged  with obstruction of justice is not a  strong position it's a weak position now  to the first part could a president be  charged with obstruction differing  opinions about this when you look at the  articles of impeachment filed against  Richard Nixon they started by saying  that Nixon obstructed and impeded the  administration of justice Bob Woodward  believes that this is not really a  settled issue but said that  realistically the only actual path  forward for Trump's removal would be  impeachment or resignation and that you  certainly shouldn't be counting on  getting the President on criminal  obstruction of justice charges but  remember Bill Clinton was impeached for  perjury and obstruction of justice and  what are we coming to we're coming to  endless and far-reaching investigations  of everyone at every level here because  it's not just Trump we learned about  katie mcfarland we learned about jeff  sessions we learned about Mike Flynn and  Jared Kushner in pence the Republican  Party held years of hearings over  Benghazi for Hillary Clinton they  impeached Bill Clinton for lying about  oral sex they flipped 